From 216ad8b44fc9888dec1fec3b8e573ed4910eef95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:04:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09/13] Round 9: Reuse the lane effort increment while the step
 repeats

In the lockstep lane kernel the effort increment h * w / 6 depends only
on the shared step h and the per-segment force weight w. Keep it per
lane and recompute it only when h differs from the cached step or a new
segment starts. The grid step repeats exactly over long stretches, so
most steps skip one division per lane. The reused value comes from the
same operations; records stay byte-identical, which the lockstep and
vector-kernel unit tests check against the scalar kernel.

Workload: domain (48 full records, PD control, 4,000 RK4 steps each,
one worker).
Before median: 0.7316 ms. After median: 0.6655 ms. Speedup: 1.10x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
